  "narrative": {
    "intro": "KBR Services has $612M in federal contract obligations for FY2026 to date, spread across 104 awards with an average award size of $5.9M. Obligations are down 27.8% year over year. KBR Services received most of its FY2026 obligations from the Department of Defense, which obligated $601M. Facilities Support Services is the largest market for KBR Services in FY2026 to date, with $512M in obligations. Historical obligations show a peak at $2.1B in FY22 and a decline to $847M in FY25 before the current-year total of $612M. Other FY2026 markets include Commercial and Industrial Machinery and Equipment Repair and Maintenance at $66.6M, Hotels (except Casino Hotels) and Motels at $15M, and Engineering Services at $7.8M. The page reports award counts and values rather than total contract ceilings, and current-year totals are partial because the fiscal year is still in progress.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How did KBR Services perform in FY2026 to date?",
        "body": "KBR Services has $612M in obligations and 104 awards, with an average award size of $5.9M. Obligations are down 27.8% year over year, reflecting a continuation of the decline from earlier fiscal years after a $2.1B peak in FY22."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are the biggest customers and what markets dominate?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the largest buyer, obligating $601M in FY2026 to date. Facilities Support Services leads the markets with $512M, followed by Commercial and Industrial Machinery and Equipment Repair and Maintenance at $66.6M."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does KBR Services make from federal contracts?",
      "a": "KBR Services has $612M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The company won 104 awards this fiscal year so far, with an average award size of $5.9M, and obligations are down 27.8% year over year."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies buy from KBR Services?",
      "a": "The Department of Defense is the primary buyer, obligating $601M. Other buying agencies in FY2026 to date include the Department of State with $5.3M and the National Science Foundation with $5M."
